{"slug":"extension","fork":"Blockchains/extension","upstream":"tahowallet/extension","branch":"main","commit":"785303c74da2606eb169a073956a03818b3fe8d3","indexed_at":"2026-10-04T16:38:34Z","category":"wallets","description":"Taho, the community owned and operated Web3 wallet.","readme_summary":"Taho is a community owned and operated Web3 wallet, built as a browser extension. Today's Web3 landscape is dominated by a single wallet and a single infrastructure provider, both owned by a single conglomerate. These facts undermine the censorship resistance of Ethereum today... and they're also against Web3's spirit of community ownership. - Fairly launched \u2696\ufe0f - Sustainably aligned with users \ud83e\udd32 - Wholly owned by the community \ud83d\udc6a Once the build is running, you can install the extension in your browser of choice: - Firefox instructions - Chrome, Brave, Edge, and Opera instructions - Note that these instructions are for Chrome, but substituting `brave://extensions` or `edge://extensions` or `opera://extensions` for `chrome://extensions` depending on browser should get you to the same buttons.","install_commands":["npm install -g yarn # if you don't have yarn globally installed","yarn install # install all dependencies; rerun with --ignore-scripts if","yarn start # start a continuous webpack build that will auto-update with changes","yarn start --config-name firefox","yarn start --config-name firefox --config-name brave","yarn start --config-name chrome","npm config set python /usr/bin/python3","yarn install","yarn start","yarn version --patch # bump patch version, e.g. 0.0.5->0.0.6","yarn version --minor # bump minor version, e.g. 0.1.5->0.2.0","yarn build # create a production build of the extension","yarn lint # lint all sources in all projects","yarn lint-fix # auto-fix any auto-fixable lint issues","yarn test # run all tests in all projects","git clone https://github.com:tallycash/extension.git tallyho-firefox"],"languages_bytes":{"TypeScript